                    embeddings and &ldquo;massive activation&rdquo; channels (documented in KVQuant and the
                    massive-activations literature). One hot channel inside a group inflates the range,
                    and the scale is range/15. Toy group with one outlier:
                  </p>
                  <p class="kvq-mono-block">
                    [0.03, −0.05, 0.02, −0.01, 0.04, 0.01, −0.02, <strong>4.80</strong>]<br />
                    s = 4.85 / 15 = 0.323 · z = 0<br />
                    every normal value: round(x / 0.323) = 0 → decodes to exactly 0.0
                  </p>
                  <p>Seven of eight channels are erased. The outlier is fine; everything near it dies.</p>
