                    At 2 bits a group has 4 codes → 3 steps; round-to-nearest noise per value is ~4×
                    the INT4 case, and accuracy falls off a cliff rather than degrading gracefully —
                    long-context retrieval and multi-step reasoning go first. Working 2-bit systems are
                    never &ldquo;the same recipe, smaller grid&rdquo;: they add non-uniform (quantile/learned)
                    levels, isolate outliers into a sparse FP16 side-band (KVQuant), tighten groups, and
                    keep a recent-token FP16 window (KIVI). Textbook INT4 is nearly free; 2-bit is a
                    research area.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </details>

              <details class="kvq-fail">
